0001- /*
0002- FUNCTION
0003- 	<<strlen>>---character string length
0004- INDEX
0005- 	strlen
0006- ANSI_SYNOPSIS
0007- 	#include <string.h>
0008- 	size_t strlen(const char *<[str]>);
0009- TRAD_SYNOPSIS
0010- 	#include <string.h>
0011- 	size_t strlen(<[str]>)
0012- 	char *<[src]>;
0013- DESCRIPTION
0014- 	The <<strlen>> function works out the length of the string
0015- 	starting at <<*<[str]>>> by counting chararacters until it
0016- 	reaches a <<NULL>> character.
0017- RETURNS
0018- 	<<strlen>> returns the character count.
0019- PORTABILITY
0020- <<strlen>> is ANSI C.
0021- <<strlen>> requires no supporting OS subroutines.
0022- QUICKREF
0023- 	strlen ansi pure
0024- */
